<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Emotion Encoded | Artificial Intelligence in Orthopaedic Surgery: Mr. Derrick E. Lousaing</title>
    
    <script src="https://cdn.tailwindcss.com"></script>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@200;400;700;900&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
    
    <style>
        body { 
            font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; 
            background-color: #000; 
            color: #fff; 
            margin: 0;
            -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
            overflow-x: hidden;
            width: 100%;
        }

        .nav-item {
            color: rgba(255,255,255,0.4);
            text-decoration: none;
            font-size: 10px;
            letter-spacing: 0.3em;
            text-transform: uppercase;
            transition: all 0.4s ease;
            font-weight: 400;
        }
        .nav-item:hover { 
            color: #fff; 
            letter-spacing: 0.4em; 
        }

        .glass-card {
            background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.02);
            backdrop-filter: blur(25px);
            -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(25px);
            border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);
            border-radius: 30px;
            max-width: 900px;
            width: 95%;
            margin: 0 auto;
            box-shadow: 0 40px 100px rgba(0,0,0,0.7);
            overflow: hidden;
        }

        .card-body {
            padding: 30px 20px;
        }
        @media (min-width: 768px) {
            .card-body {
                padding: 50px 60px;
            }
        }

        .reveal {
            opacity: 0;
            transform: translateY(20px);
            transition: all 1s cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1);
        }
        .reveal.active {
            opacity: 1;
            transform: translateY(0);
        }

        .q-box {
            border-left: 2px solid #2dd4bf;
            padding-left: 20px;
            margin-bottom: 20px;
            text-align: left;
        }

        .ans-box {
            background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03);
            border-radius: 20px;
            padding: 25px;
            margin-bottom: 30px;
            border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05);
            text-align: left;
        }

        .verdict-box {
            background: rgba(45, 212, 191, 0.03);
            border: 1px solid rgba(45, 212, 191, 0.15);
            border-radius: 20px;
            padding: 30px;
            margin-top: 50px;
            text-align: left;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

    <section style="
        min-height: 100vh;
        padding: 40px 0;
        background: radial-gradient(circle at top, #0d0d0d 0%, #000 100%);
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        align-items: center;
    ">

        <nav class="reveal active" style="
            display: flex; 
            flex-wrap: wrap; 
            justify-content: center; 
            gap: 20px; 
            margin-bottom: 40px;
            padding-bottom: 20px;
            border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.05);
            width: 90%;
            max-width: 900px;
        ">
            <a href="index.html" class="nav-item">Home</a>
            <a href="about.html" class="nav-item">About</a>
            <a href="Methodsanddata.html" class="nav-item">Methods</a>
            <a href="DataAnalysisquantitative.html" class="nav-item">PrePrint</a>
            <a href="ethicalguidelines.html" class="nav-item">Ethics</a>
            <a href="AI-Perception-Briefs.html" class="nav-item" style="color: #2dd4bf; border-bottom: 1px solid #2dd4bf;">Findings</a>
            <a href="contact.html" class="nav-item">Contact</a>
        </nav>

        <div class="glass-card reveal">
            
            <div style="width: 100%; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); background: #000; display: flex; justify-content: center;">
                <img src="images/article70.jpg" 
                     alt="Artificial Intelligence in Orthopaedic Surgery - Discussion with Mr. Derrick E. Lousaing" 
                     style="width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; object-fit: contain;">
            </div>

            <div class="card-body">
                
                <span style="font-size: 9px; letter-spacing: 0.4em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #2dd4bf; margin-bottom: 12px; display: block; text-align: left;">
                    ENCODEDEMOTION.ORG
                </span>
                
                <h1 style="
                    font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 6vw, 2.5rem);
                    font-weight: 900;
                    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
                    line-height: 1.1;
                    margin-bottom: 35px;
                    background: linear-gradient(to right, #ffffff, #a1a1aa);
                    -webkit-background-clip: text;
                    -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent;
                    text-align: left;
                ">
                    Artificial Intelligence in Orthopaedic Surgery: Surgical Precision and Workflow Automation
                </h1>

                <h2 style="font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 700; color: #fff; margin-bottom: 20px; text-align: left;">
                    Mr. Derrick E. Lousaing — Consultant Orthopaedic Surgeon
                </h2>

                <p style="color: rgba(255,255,255,0.8); line-height: 1.7; font-size: 1.1rem; margin-bottom: 30px; text-align: left;">
                    This research brief examines trust calibration between human surgical mastery and software tools in high-stakes operating room environments, based on a structured discussion with Mr. Derrick E. Lousaing.
                </p>

                <p style="color: rgba(255,255,255,0.8); line-height: 1.7; font-size: 1.1rem; margin-bottom: 30px; text-align: left;">
                    Mr. Derrick E. Lousaing is a Consultant Orthopaedic Surgeon with over thirty-five years of extensive experience, specializing in joint preservation, lower limb reconstruction, and complex hip and knee arthroplasty. Co-founder of the Fracture and Orthopaedic Clinic in Trinidad and Tobago, he pioneered regional joint replacement techniques and performs approximately 150 total joint replacements annually. Committed to continuous training, surgical precision, and advanced clinical education, he remains a leading authority in Caribbean orthopaedic care.
                </p>

                <div class="q-box">
                    <p style="color: rgba(255,255,255,0.6); font-style: italic; line-height: 1.6;">
                        Question: Do you use any AI tools like ChatGPT or Gemini for any part of your work right now?
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="ans-box">
                    <p style="color: #fff; line-height: 1.7; font-size: 1.05rem;">
                        "Yes we use a program called Heidi for consultation and this can integrate with our EMR to do a number of task"
                    </p>
                </div>

                <p style="color: rgba(255,255,255,0.8); line-height: 1.7; font-size: 1.1rem; margin-bottom: 30px; text-align: left;">
                    This insight highlights the pragmatic boundary between consumer chat applications and specialized clinical integration software. Surgical environments are actively adopting workflow automation, but strictly for administrative relief and documentation management rather than direct anatomical decision-making. The integration of AI in high-stakes specialties begins at the administrative bottleneck of patient charting.
                </p>

                <div class="q-box">
                    <p style="color: rgba(255,255,255,0.6); font-style: italic; line-height: 1.6;">
                        Question: Would you rely on an AI system to actively monitor your surgical precision in real time, or do you prefer it to stay entirely focused on background data management?
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="ans-box">
                    <p style="color: #fff; line-height: 1.7; font-size: 1.05rem;">
                        "We have a combination of the two but no fully integrated AI system for active monitoring"
                    </p>
                </div>

                <p style="color: rgba(255,255,255,0.8); line-height: 1.7; font-size: 1.1rem; margin-bottom: 30px; text-align: left;">
                    In complex joint preservation and lower limb reconstruction, the margin for error is microscopic. While digital systems organize background metrics, physical execution relies completely on the spatial awareness, tactile feedback, and internalized muscle memory of the human surgeon. Active mechanical monitoring cannot yet replicate the nuanced adaptations required for unexpected anatomical variations.
                </p>

                <div class="q-box">
                    <p style="color: rgba(255,255,255,0.6); font-style: italic; line-height: 1.6;">
                        Question: If an error is about to happen mid-procedure, would you want the system to interrupt you with a warning, or quietly record details for later review?
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="ans-box">
                    <p style="color: #fff; line-height: 1.7; font-size: 1.05rem;">
                        "If we were using it then we would prefer the system to interrupt an error before it occurs"
                    </p>
                </div>

                <p style="color: rgba(255,255,255,0.8); line-height: 1.7; font-size: 1.1rem; margin-bottom: 30px; text-align: left;">
                    In major orthopaedic surgery, recording a mistake for later review offers zero value to the patient on the table. For an algorithmic intervention to hold practical utility in an active theatre, it must function as an immediate safety net, placing immense demands on system reliability to avoid dangerous false-positive distractions.
                </p>

                <div class="q-box">
                    <p style="color: rgba(255,255,255,0.6); font-style: italic; line-height: 1.6;">
                        Question: Do you worry that relying too much on AI will make younger surgeons lose their touch in emergencies?
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="ans-box">
                    <p style="color: #fff; line-height: 1.7; font-size: 1.05rem;">
                        "yes"
                    </p>
                </div>

                <p style="color: rgba(255,255,255,0.8); line-height: 1.7; font-size: 1.1rem; margin-bottom: 30px; text-align: left;">
                    Absolute dependence on automated guidance risks eroding the raw, instinctive problem-solving skills required when trainees face sudden intraoperative crises. Decades of surgical mastery are built upon weathering high-pressure complications manually. If younger practitioners bypass foundational crisis navigation by trusting algorithms to dictate solutions, the core resilience and adaptive intuition of the workforce face a severe generational threat.
                </p>

                <div class="verdict-box">
                    <p style="color: #2dd4bf; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; text-transform: uppercase; font-size: 0.8rem; letter-spacing: 0.1em;">RESEARCH IMPLICATIONS</p>
                    <p style="color: rgba(255,255,255,0.9); line-height: 1.7;">
                        The interview with Mr. Derrick E. Lousaing reinforces the core thesis of our research track regarding procedural domains. While administrative automation like EMR-integrated scribing tools are embraced to streamline clinic hours, high-stakes surgical specialists draw a hard line against autonomous intervention. Real-time surgical tools must act as immediate, interruptive safety guardrails rather than passive logs, ensuring the preservation of foundational human expertise and emergency resilience among the next generation of surgeons.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="reveal" style="text-align: center; margin-top: 50px;">
                    <p style="font-family: 'Courier New', monospace; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.2); font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 0.1em;">
                        Sonrisa Watts // Emotion Encoded // 2026
                    </p>
                </div>

            </div>
        </div>

    </section>

    <script>
        window.addEventListener('load', () => {
            const observer = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
                entries.forEach(entry => {
                    if (entry.isIntersecting) {
                        entry.target.classList.add('active');
                    }
                });
            }, { threshold: 0.05 });

            document.querySelectorAll('.reveal').forEach(el => observer.observe(el));
        });
    </script>
</body>
</html>
